  <story>
    <asA>developer</asA>
    <iWant>phase transitions validated against maturity requirements before allowing progression</iWant>
    <soThat>the system prevents premature jumps (e.g., coding before architecture is defined)</soThat>
    <tasks>
      <task id="1" ac="1">Define phase gate rules as queryable configuration
        <subtask>Create /home/ubuntu/scripts/lib/phase-gates.mjs defining all 6 phase gate transitions with their requirements</subtask>
        <subtask>Each gate rule specifies: source phase, target phase, required node types, minimum maturity per type, minimum count per type</subtask>
        <subtask>Gate rules: Discovery to Planning (brainstorm/brief at 0.4, count 1); Planning to Solutioning (prd at 0.6, count 1, requirement at 0.4, count 1); Solutioning to Implementation (architecture at 0.6, count 1, tech-spec at 0.4, count 1); Implementation to QA (code avg maturity 0.6 + all stories completed); QA to Release (test-plan at 0.6 + critical tests passing); Release to Support (deployment successful + release notes)</subtask>
        <subtask>Export function getGateRequirements(sourcePhase, targetPhase) returning the rules</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="2" ac="2">Implement gate check logic via Memgraph queries
        <subtask>Create /home/ubuntu/scripts/lib/check-phase-gate.mjs that queries Memgraph to evaluate gate requirements</subtask>
        <subtask>For each gate rule, run Cypher query to find nodes of required type in source phase and check maturity scores</subtask>
        <subtask>Aggregate results: count qualifying nodes, compute average maturity where needed, identify nodes below threshold</subtask>
        <subtask>Return gate result object: {passed: boolean, warnings: [{rule, actual, required, missingNodes}]}</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="3" ac="3">Implement soft gate warning system
        <subtask>When gate check returns passed: false, emit a structured warning (not an error) to the pipeline output</subtask>
        <subtask>Warning format: Phase gate warning: {sourcePhase} to {targetPhase} Missing: {list of unmet requirements with current vs required maturity}</subtask>
        <subtask>Pipeline continues after warning (soft gate, not hard blocker)</subtask>
        <subtask>Warning included in pipeline job result (DynamoDB futurator-agent-jobs) so it surfaces in Labs UI</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="4" ac="4">Track gate status in pending-work.md
        <subtask>After each gate check, update knowledge/system/pending-work.md with a Phase Gates section</subtask>
        <subtask>List each phase transition attempted with unmet requirements</subtask>
        <subtask>Include specific nodes needing maturity improvement with current and target maturity scores</subtask>
        <subtask>Remove entries from pending-work.md when gate requirements are subsequently met</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="5" ac="5,6">Log gate checks and integrate into compilation flow
        <subtask>Log every gate check in knowledge/log.md: timestamp, projectId, attempted transition, gate status (passed/warned), missing items</subtask>
        <subtask>Integrate gate checks into pre-dev compilation step (Story 4.1): after a new node is created, determine which phase it belongs to and check if upstream phase gate is satisfied</subtask>
        <subtask>Phase detection logic: infer target phase from article type being created (prd means Planning phase, check Discovery to Planning gate)</subtask>
        <subtask>Gate checks also run at epic transition points (planning to solutioning, solutioning to implementation)</subtask>
      </task>
    </tasks>
  </story>

  <acceptanceCriteria>
    <criterion id="1">The system enforces the phase gates defined in architecture doc section 6.3: Discovery to Planning requires at least 1 brainstorm/brief node at maturity >= 0.4; Planning to Solutioning requires PRD at maturity >= 0.6 and requirements at >= 0.4; Solutioning to Implementation requires architecture at >= 0.6 and tech spec at >= 0.4; Implementation to QA requires all epic stories completed and code nodes at >= 0.6 avg; QA to Release requires test plan at >= 0.6 and all critical tests passing; Release to Support requires deployment successful and release notes generated</criterion>
    <criterion id="2">When a pipeline or agent session attempts to create nodes in a downstream phase, the system checks if gate requirements are met by querying node maturity in Memgraph</criterion>
    <criterion id="3">If gate requirements are NOT met, a warning is emitted listing what is missing — the pipeline continues (soft gate, not a hard blocker)</criterion>
    <criterion id="4">Gate status is tracked in knowledge/system/pending-work.md with a section listing unmet gate requirements per phase transition</criterion>
    <criterion id="5">Phase gate checks are logged in knowledge/log.md with timestamp, attempted transition, gate status (passed/warned), and missing items</criterion>
    <criterion id="6">Gate checks run as part of the pre-dev compilation step (Story 4.1) — evaluated whenever a new node is created in a phase that requires upstream phase completion</criterion>
  </acceptanceCriteria>

