  <constraints>
    <constraint type="architecture">Phase gates are SOFT gates (warnings), not hard blockers. This is personal developer tooling, not enterprise governance. The system warns when skipping ahead but does not prevent pipeline execution.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Gate checks evaluate nodes with status: active only. Flagged, superseded, and pruned nodes do not count toward gate satisfaction.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">The 7-phase model is: Discovery, Planning, Solutioning, Implementation, QA, Release, Support. Gate checks are most valuable during pre-dev phases (first 4 transitions) where skipping ahead is most common and costly.</constraint>
    <constraint type="convention">Gate check results are stored in DynamoDB (futurator-agent-jobs) via the existing ValidationResult interface for UI display, and in knowledge/system/pending-work.md for wiki-based tracking.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">Requires Story 4.1 (Document Generation Compilation Hook) as the integration point for gate checks during pre-dev compilation.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">Requires Epic 1 complete (Memgraph with schema, maturity scores populated on nodes by compilation steps).</constraint>
  </constraints>

